<title>ITALY: Italy rejects talk of tax on short-term bills.</title>
<headline>Italy rejects talk of tax on short-term bills.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government does not plan to tax short-term bills (BOTs), the undersecretary at Prime Minister Romano Prodi's office said.</p>
<p>Recent news reports have speculated that the government was planning to tax BOTs as part of the so-called &quot;Euro Tax&quot;, a number of fiscal initiatives yet to be spelt out which are designed to raise 13 trillion lire in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The government...has never remotely considered any measures such as the taxation of BOTs,&quot; undersecretary Enrico Micheli said in a statement. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
